      {
        "id": "p23-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(x-3)(x^2+6x-8)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3,\\ -3+\\sqrt{17},\\ -3-\\sqrt{17}$",
          "worked": "$x=3$ or $x^2+6x-8=0$.\nFor the quadratic, the quadratic formula gives\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{6^2-4(1)(-8)}}{2}\\\\x&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{68}}{2}\\\\x&=-3\\pm\\sqrt{17}.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x=3,\\ -3+\\sqrt{17},\\ -3-\\sqrt{17}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(x+5)^2(3x^2-2x-2)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-5,\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt7}{3},\\ \\frac{1-\\sqrt7}{3}$",
          "worked": "$x=-5$ or $3x^2-2x-2=0$.\nFor the quadratic,\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{(-2)^2-4(3)(-2)}}{6}\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{28}}{6}\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt7}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x=-5,\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt7}{3},\\ \\frac{1-\\sqrt7}{3}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$5x^3(x-7)(x+6)(x^2+2x+5)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0,\\ 7,\\ -6$",
          "worked": "The linear and power factors give $x=0,\\ 7,\\ -6$.\n$$x^2+2x+5=(x+1)^2+4>0$$\nfor every real $x$, so this quadratic supplies no real solutions.\nThus $x=0,\\ 7,\\ -6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$-2(x-2)^2(x-5)^4(x^2-10)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2,\\ 5,\\ \\sqrt{10},\\ -\\sqrt{10}$",
          "worked": "$x=2$ or $x=5$ or $x^2-10=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=10\\\\x&=\\pm\\sqrt{10}.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x=2,\\ 5,\\ \\sqrt{10},\\ -\\sqrt{10}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
